# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sTiles — public repo (GitHub Pages site under docs/ + R/Python bindings).
# Platform binaries ship as GitHub Release assets, never committed here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Markdown docs are kept internal; the site (docs/) is the documentation.
# (.gitkeep files are preserved below so binary-drop dirs still exist.)
# README.md is the exception: it is the repo landing page and points at the site.
# The per-package READMEs are exceptions too. Python puts its PyPI description
# in pyproject.toml and R puts its in DESCRIPTION, but Project.toml has no
# description field at all, so for Julia the README file is the only thing the
# package page can show.
*.md
!/README.md
!/julia/README.md
!/python/README.md
!**/.gitkeep

# Python build / cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
python/build/
python/dist/
python/*.egg-info/

# Julia: resolved environment is machine-specific; vendored solvers live in deps/
julia/Manifest.toml
julia/deps/**

# R build / personal history
**/.Rhistory
R/**/*.o
R/**/*.so
R/**/*.Rcheck/
R/sTiles/src/Makevars
R/sTiles/sTiles_*.tar.gz

# Compiled objects / archives / logs
*.o
*.a
*.log

# ctest compiled binaries (sources committed, build outputs not)
ctest/test_stiles
ctest/scale_stiles
ctest/run_mtx

# Platform libraries — distributed as GitHub Release assets, not committed
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.dll.a
_libs/**
!_libs/**/.gitkeep
R/sTiles/inst/solver/**
!R/sTiles/inst/solver/README.md

# CI artifact zips + their extracted trees (fetched, never committed)
binaries/*.zip
binaries/libstiles-*/

# Dropped from the public repo (kept locally for reference)
prebuilt/
examples/
# ... except the Julia package's own examples, which its README walks through
# (a directory must be re-included before the files inside it can be)
!/julia/examples/
docs/suits/old_site/

# local release tooling, not part of the published package
extract_binaries.sh
release.sh
sync_binaries.sh
